{
  "description": "THE ANTI-RETROACTIVITY RULE, across the repository boundary. The code was committed three hours ago; the declaration that would legalise it landed one hour ago. The ordering IS the violation — without this the pattern 'commit the code, declare the territory afterwards' is a permanently green gate, which is what feature 012's phase 1 review found and the owner adjudicated on 2026-09-09. The message quotes the commit's own instant back, which is why the harness normalises <DATE> at all.",
  "defaultBranch": "main",
  "commits": [
    {
      "branch": "main",
      "message": "init",
      "hoursAgo": 5,
      "write": {
        "README.md": "fixture kit\n",
        "kit-adoption.json": [
          "{",
          "  \"kitVersion\": \"0.9.0\",",
          "  \"codeRepos\": [\"code-repo\"]",
          "}"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "branch": "001-thing",
      "message": "spec: 001 thing",
      "hoursAgo": 1,
      "write": {
        "specs/001-thing/spec.md": [
          "# Feature Specification: Thing",
          "",
          "**Feature Branch**: `001-thing`",
          "**Status**: Approved 2026-01-01 (owner: fixture)",
          "**Delivery Level**: Standard",
          "",
          "## Requirements",
          "",
          "- **FR-001**: System MUST do the thing."
        ],
        "specs/001-thing/plan.md": [
          "# Implementation Plan: Thing",
          "",
          "**Gate Batching**: none",
          "**Gate Certification**: user-run",
          "",
          "## Summary",
          "",
          "One phase."
        ],
        "specs/001-thing/tasks.md": [
          "# Tasks: Thing",
          "",
          "## Phase 1: The thing",
          "",
          "**Territory**:",
          "",
          "- `code-repo/src/**`",
          "",
          "- [ ] T001 Do the thing."
        ]
      }
    }
  ],
  "checkout": "001-thing",
  "nestedRepos": {
    "code-repo": {
      "defaultBranch": "main",
      "commits": [
        {
          "branch": "main",
          "message": "init",
          "hoursAgo": 4,
          "write": {
            "README.md": "code\n"
          }
        },
        {
          "branch": "001-thing",
          "message": "phase 1: the thing",
          "hoursAgo": 3,
          "write": {
            "src/a.txt": "a\n"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  }
}
